{"name":"Deep Sea","hex":"#167e65","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deep sea","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The deeper part of the sea or ocean in which no light penetrates.","An open sea."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep_sea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Deep sea","blocks":[{"text":"The deep sea is broadly defined as the ocean depth where light begins to fade, at an approximate depth of 200 m (660 ft) or the point of transition from continental shelves to continental slopes. Conditions within the deep sea are a combination of low temperatures, darkness, and high pressure. The deep sea is considered the least explored Earth biome as the extreme conditions make the environment difficult to access and explore."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Schematic_representation_of_pelagic_and_benthic_zones.jpg/330px-Schematic_representation_of_pelagic_and_benthic_zones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_sea"},{"title":"Deep Sea (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Deep Sea is a 2023 Chinese 3D animated fantasy film, written and directed by Tian Xiaopeng, who previously directed Monkey King: Hero Is Back, co-produced by his company October Media and Coloroom Pictures."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/99/Deep_Sea_2023_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_Sea_(film)"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px